# Line endings: always LF ("\n") for text files, on every computer.
# Why? DVC remembers an md5 hash of every code file a stage depends on.
# Windows Git (core.autocrlf=true) would check files out with CRLF ("\r\n"),
# which changes the hash, so DVC would think the code changed and re-run
# every stage. With LF everywhere, Windows, Linux (CI) and DagsHub agree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never touch their bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.joblib binary
*.zip binary
